                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_02\n\nCONFIDENCE: MEDIUM\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes StartUpView.java's anonymous IPlayerClientListener implementation of\nonUpdateCheckpointDirection() (no arguments) to onUpdateCheckpointDirection(Position pos),\nadding an import for at.fhv.audioracer.core.util.Position. This is a classic \"build error\"\nfix: the @Override-annotated method in StartUpView.java no longer matched the interface\nmethod's signature, so the project failed to compile until the parameter was added.\n\nTracing the origin of that exact code, candidate_02 is the commit that first created the\nIPlayerClientListener interface (with the method declared as `void onUpdateCheckpointDirection();`,\nno arguments) and simultaneously introduced the anonymous listener implementation inside\nStartUpView.java with the matching no-argument override:\n`public void onUpdateCheckpointDirection() { ... }`.\n\nAcross the remaining candidates (03-07), this specific line in StartUpView.java is never\ntouched again, and no candidate updates the interface's onUpdateCheckpointDirection() to add\na Position parameter (candidate_06 only adds a no-op `Adapter` class to the interface that\nstill uses the original no-argument signature). This means the no-argument implementation in\nStartUpView.java, first written in candidate_02, is the code that eventually became stale\nrelative to the interface contract and had to be patched by the fix commit. Since no other\ncandidate re-touches or introduces a conflicting signature for this method before the fix, and\ncandidate_02 is the sole place where this problematic (later-to-be-broken) implementation was\nfirst written, it is the most likely bug-introducing commit under SZZ blame-based reasoning\n(git blame on the removed line in the fix diff would resolve to candidate_02).\n\nNote: candidate_08's diff is textually identical to the fix commit's diff (same before/after\nblob hashes), meaning candidate_08 essentially duplicates the fix itself rather than\nintroducing the bug, so it was excluded from consideration despite touching the same line.\n"
